  "name": "aban — Publish Fanout",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## aban Publish-Fanout\n\nEmpfängt den Webhook von `social/post.py` (Feld `PUBLISH_WEBHOOK_URL`) und postet an\nLinkedIn, X und Mastodon.\n\n**Einrichten:**\n1. Workflow importieren.\n2. In jedem Post-Node deine **Credential** verbinden (LinkedIn / X OAuth, Mastodon-Token).\n3. Workflow **aktivieren**.\n4. Im Webhook-Node die **Production-URL** kopieren → als GitHub-Secret `PUBLISH_WEBHOOK_URL` setzen.\n\nDie eingehenden Felder liegen unter `{{ $json.body }}`: `text`, `url`, `id`, `tags`.\nNicht gebrauchte Plattform-Nodes einfach löschen oder deaktivieren.",
        "height": 320,
        "width": 380
      },
      "id": "note1",
      "name": "Anleitung",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [-40, 0]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "path": "aban-publish",
        "responseMode": "onReceived",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "webhook1",
      "name": "Webhook (von post.py)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [420, 200],
      "webhookId": "aban-publish"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Baut den Post-Text aus dem Webhook-Body (text + optional url).\nconst b = ($input.first().json.body) || $input.first().json || {};\nconst url = b.url ? `\\n${b.url}` : '';\nreturn [{ json: { text: `${b.text || ''}${url}`.trim(), raw: b } }];"
      },
      "id": "format1",
      "name": "Text bauen",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [660, 200]
    },
